# Dictionary source files are committed verbatim so that a shipped build can be
# reproduced exactly (D-41, D-55). Three of the four sources have no version
# history — a past JMdict cannot be re-fetched — so these files ARE the version
# record.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion. Without it git would rewrite LF
# to CRLF on Windows checkouts, changing the bytes and therefore the SHA-256
# recorded in sources.lock.json — defeating the entire point of committing them.
#
# `-diff` marks them binary for diff purposes, so `git diff`, the GitHub PR view
# and the API all report "Binary files differ" instead of emitting 12 MB of
# furigana alignments. This matters beyond readability: an automated reviewer
# reading these files consumed an entire token budget in a single run before the
# review workflow was made manual-only.
#
# `linguist-generated` additionally collapses them in the GitHub PR view and
# excludes them from language statistics.

tools/dictbuild/data/**      -text -diff linguist-generated
tools/dictbuild/baseline/**  -text -diff linguist-generated

# The Gradle wrapper.
#
# `gradlew` is a POSIX shell script and MUST keep LF endings. Git's autocrlf on
# Windows would otherwise rewrite it to CRLF on checkout, and Linux CI then
# fails with a "bad interpreter: no such file or directory" error that names the
# shell rather than the line endings — an expensive thing to debug.
#
# `gradlew.bat` is the opposite: a Windows batch file, which wants CRLF.
#
# Both are marked `-diff linguist-generated` for the same reason as the datasets
# above: they are generated boilerplate nobody hand-edits, and between them they
# are ~15k tokens. Collapsing them keeps them out of PR diffs, out of GitHub's
# language statistics, and out of any reviewer's context — automated or human.
# To change them, regenerate with `gradle wrapper`, never patch by hand.
gradlew        text eol=lf   -diff linguist-generated
gradlew.bat    text eol=crlf -diff linguist-generated
*.jar          -text -diff linguist-generated

# Generated artifacts, wherever they land.
*.db      -text -diff linguist-generated
*.db-wal  -text -diff
*.db-journal -text -diff
*.gz      -text -diff linguist-generated
*.tsv     -text -diff linguist-generated
